body:
Part of #372; needs the machine-file axis direction (#373).

When a machine axis is inverted, the controller's coordinate system is the mirror of the CAM frame in that axis. The post must translate, not just negate:
- write the inverted axis's coordinates and its arc-centre offset (I/J/K) with the opposite sign;
- an arc in a plane that contains exactly one inverted axis reverses its sense in controller coordinates: **G2 <-> G3** (two inverted axes in the plane cancel);
- cutter compensation side swaps the same way: **G41 <-> G42**;
- work-offset values and any probe / tool-length data that carry that axis follow the same sign rule.

Refuse by name (until verified per dialect): helical/thread cycles, polar/G12.1, rotary or 4/5-axis motion involving the inverted axis, and any canned cycle whose direction depends on axis sense.

**Done means:** implemented in the post engine (one place, not per script) or per shipped `.cps` with a shared helper; conformance goldens for an inverted-X Fanuc and Haas program covering lines, G2/G3 in G17/G18/G19, I/J/K, G41/G42; a test that a physically identical path is produced (simulate the controller's interpretation of the posted program and compare with the CAM path); refusals pinned.

Found while fixing #91. Verify's rapid law (d) (`crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs`, the `dx*dx + dy*dy <= z_tol^2` arm) skips EVERY vertical rapid as "a retract through the tool's own kerf" - including rapids going DOWN into uncut stock. #91 closes the drilling case at generation (an R plane below the stock top is refused by name), but the law itself still lets any other op's vertical rapid into declared stock post silently.

Proof from the existing suites, with the held verify patch below applied (a downward vertical rapid whose `to.z` is below `Rest::surface_before` at its column, inside the stock, is `RapidInStock`):

- `crates/app/tests/posting.rs` `contour_and_drill`: box stock 100x100x10 (top Z 10), Contour1 with clearance 10 / retract 8 over a 5 mm part - move 1 is a rapid 10 -> 8, 2 mm into the declared stock. Today it posts silently; with the patch, 6 posting tests fail on `RapidInStock { at: 1 }`.
- `crates/app/tests/operations.rs` `the_shell_switch_sends_the_pocket_to_the_offset_engine`: box stock 60x60x20 (top Z 20), Pocket3D clearance 10 - move 1 rapids down inside the stock. Fails with `RapidInStock { at: 1 }` under the patch.

Both fixtures are real collisions by their own declared stock (the tool rapids below the stock top), so the fix is the law plus fixture repairs; the blast radius over the rest of the app/ui suites and the .nc goldens is unmeasured - which is why it was held out of #91.

Held patch (sim, 10 lines; peck re-entries above their own earlier plunge stay clean because the cut-order chords acquit them):

```diff
             if dx * dx + dy * dy <= cx.z_tol * cx.z_tol {
-                continue; // vertical retract through the tool's own kerf
+                let down = m.to.z < m.from.z - cx.z_tol;
+                if down && rest.in_stock(a) && m.to.z < rest.surface_before(a, i) - cx.z_tol {
+                    warns.push(Warning::RapidInStock { at: i });
+                }
+                continue;
             }
```

A verify-level test file was written for it (4 tests: R plane under stock top convicts; R over the stock top is clean; peck re-entry above its plunge clean; re-entry past its plunge convicts) - all green with the patch, `cargo test -p camcraft-sim` otherwise unchanged (all green).

Done means: the law lands, every suite that trips it is checked fixture-by-fixture (real collision -> fix the fixture; a false conviction -> fix the law), goldens re-verified.
